sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer
    participant System as Ticket System
    participant Triage as Triage Agent
    participant CRM
    participant Tech as Technical Agent
    participant Billing as Billing Agent
    participant KB as KB Agent
    participant Routing as Routing Agent
    participant Dest as Destination

    Customer->>System: Submit support ticket
    activate System

    System->>Triage: New ticket received
    activate Triage

    Triage->>CRM: Lookup customer info
    activate CRM
    CRM-->>Triage: Customer data, SLA tier
    deactivate CRM

    Note over Triage: Extract category, urgency,<br/>and determine handling type

    par Parallel Analysis
        Triage->>Tech: Analyze technical issue
        activate Tech
        and
        Triage->>Billing: Analyze billing issue
        activate Billing
        and
        Triage->>KB: Search knowledge base
        activate KB
    end

    Note over Tech,KB: All agents work independently

    Tech-->>Routing: Technical analysis result
    deactivate Tech
    Billing-->>Routing: Billing analysis result
    deactivate Billing
    KB-->>Routing: KB match or null
    deactivate KB

    Triage->>Routing: Ticket context + tier
    deactivate Triage
    activate Routing

    Note over Routing: Evaluate all results,<br/>apply routing logic & SLA

    alt High confidence solution found
        Routing->>Dest: Auto-response email
        Dest-->>Customer: Solution (40%)
    else Requires human expertise
        Routing->>Dest: Queue for L2/L3 team
        Dest-->>Customer: Acknowledgment, in queue (55%)
    else SLA risk detected
        Routing->>Dest: Escalate to manager
        Dest-->>Customer: Priority handling (5%)
    end

    deactivate Routing
    deactivate System

    Note over System,Dest: Background: SLA Escalation Agent<br/>monitors all open tickets every 5 min
